// The sovereign once parity probe: exercises every ported once symbol
// (new, done, run) end-to-end through the *builtin* spellings, exactly as
// `once_main.pkl` does for the native bodies.
//
// The one difference is the import below: importing `runtime.abi_once` is the
// measured activation condition for a `#[symbol]` body ("its module is
// imported AND codegen emits an extern reference to that name"), and every
// builtin call in this file emits the `pickle_once_*` reference. `abi_once.pkl`
// closes the wall `abi_sync.pkl`'s header reserved for this family: `once_run`
// takes a closure, and the ported `abiOnceRun` calls it through a plain
// function-type parameter (no `call_closure0` seam).
//
// Under `pickle run` the import binds the calls to the ported bodies; the
// transcript printed here must stay byte-identical to the native run (GATE6's
// `pklc_irx` arm compiles this shape with the prelinked port and irx-runs it,
// GATE12/12b's AOT arms link the Rust archive, and all three must match the
// Rust `pickle run` oracle and each other).
//
// NO FATAL: no `once_*` call ever names a wrong-kind or unknown handle (the
// `fatal: pickle: handle {n} is not a once` path is covered by the standalone
// `sl_once_kindonce` probe).

import { abiOnceNew } from runtime.abi_once

fn main() {
    var o = once_new()
    println(once_run(o, fn () { println("body one") }))
    println(once_run(o, fn () { println("body one again") }))
    println(once_done(o))
    var p = once_new()
    println(once_done(p))
    println(once_run(p, fn () { println("body two") }))
    println(once_done(p))
    println(once_done(o))
    println("once ok")
}